Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the file layout, the commit messages, the tables and
the tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

The legal text keeps its sources' own terms:

- The Saint Christopher and Nevis Constitution Order 1983 (SI 1983/881), as made (constitution/, constitution-order/):
  from legislation.gov.uk (The National Archives), read from the scanned PDF by OCR in the first build. Contains public
  sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0:
  https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/
  Source: https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/1983/881/made (scanned PDF), retrieved 30 October 2026.
  Changes made by Lexifina: the page images were converted to text by optical character recognition (Tesseract 5.4);
  marginal notes, headers and chapter headings were left out; a few misread words were corrected by hand; and the text
  was arranged as one Markdown file per provision and as git commits. Neither the National Archives nor the Government
  of Saint Kitts and Nevis endorses this repository.

- Revised Edition chapters, Acts and statutory rules and orders (laws/, nevis/, acts/, statutory-rules-and-orders/):
  official texts of the Government of Saint Christopher and Nevis, taken from secondary copies of the Government's own
  PDFs held by:
  - FAOLEX, the legislative database of the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations
    (https://www.fao.org/faolex/; records listed through ECOLEX, https://www.ecolex.org/). FAO's terms allow
    reproduction and dissemination of its material for non-commercial purposes with acknowledgement of FAO as the
    source (https://www.fao.org/contact-us/terms/en/);
  - WIPO Lex, the World Intellectual Property Organization's database of national laws
    (https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/en/members/profile/KN), whose texts are supplied by member governments; WIPO's terms
    of use (https://www.wipo.int/tools/en/disclaim.html) cover WIPO's own material, and the national laws are the
    governments' official texts.
  Each commit's Source and Source-page trailers name the PDF and the record it was taken from. A copy whose own pages
  repeat the Government's "All rights reserved. No part of this publication may be reproduced ..." notice is not used
  (see data/held.json).

- Nothing is taken from the Attorney General's Chambers' own site (lawcommission.gov.kn), whose terms of use forbid
  reproducing, republishing or reusing any part of it.

Not legal advice and not an official publication; the official texts govern.
